entry.summary:
When your app breaks, the first question is always: is it us, or is it them? If you depend on GitHub, AWS, Discord, Stripe, Cloudflare, or any major third-party service, you've probably wasted hours debugging your own code only to find out the service was down the whole time. There's a free API for this. Let me show you how to use it. DownStatus is a free, public JSON API that gives you real-time status for 90+ popular services — no API key required. curl https://isitdownstatus.com/api/status/github
Response: { "service": "github", "status": "operational", "updated_at": "2026-05-11T08:00:00Z" }
That's it. No signup, no tokens, no rate limit headers to parse. async function checkGitHubStatus() { const res = await fetch('https://isitdownstatus.com/api/status/github'); const data …
